Base on the release of "new version of iptables" about 3 years ago, at
now ver2.0 ,base on the kernel-2.6.18.8 and iptables-1.3.5 packages,
is ready for test.

Description:
iptables-TNG ( The Next Generation of iptables) An environment that
can use from different packet classification algorithms (eg. tuple) to
support large rulesets (more than 10,000 rules) for high bandwidth
networks.

the most important feature of this new version is ability of develop
and use different packet classification algorithms. in the version2
pkt_tables name space and common framework is other best feature.

for more information: https://sourceforge.net/projects/iptablestng/
Project Wiki (to see features):  http://iptablestng.wiki.sourceforge.net/

To see Ver1.0 Features and throughput tests: http://iptablestng.sourceforge.net/

To Download: http://sourceforge.net/project/showfiles.php?group_id=212533

Special thanks for Any new idea or bug and test reports.

